  "scope": "The whole original server compiled unchanged (as oracle/world-trace), started by calling the statements of GameWorld.prompt(false) one at a time in their order (ConfigParser.prePlugin/postPlugin loader by loader, start-up listeners one by one), with the world-trace boot inputs. Recorded: generator positions and the original's log lines after every call; the tables XteaParser, ObjectConfigParser, ObjectOverrideParser, MusicConfigLoader, RangedConfigLoader and ClueRewardParser leave behind, read after their own call; then each of those loaders and ShopParser again over authored inputs (CONFIG_PATH pointed at a case directory), with the exception that left it and the draws it made. Accepted only when the resulting boot record is byte-identical to the world-trace fixture's. Read-only dumps (no definition, region or DataMap lookups that create entries). Not covered: other JDKs/operating systems, the loaders' log text beyond what is printed, and every other start-up step's own tables.",
